        "kind": "adk_bug",
        "reason": "ADK logs one user message fewer than the model receives. If a request ends on a model turn, `Gemini.generate_content_async` appends a user turn (`Continue processing previous requests as instructed. ...`) before sending it, in `BaseLlm._maybe_append_user_content`. ADK logs the request's messages when it opens the inference span, before that append, so its logs miss the turn; the OTel instrumentor logs the request as sent, so it has it. In the token-threshold compaction cases the first request ends on a model turn: compaction keeps no events after its summary (`event_retention_size=0`), and a summary is a model turn."
